      "description": "Watch Coventry vs Hull City highlights and goals from Premier League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 29, 2026. The atmosphere was electric as Coventry City hosted Hull City in a Premier League clash that promised plenty of tactical intrigue. With 31,239 fans in attendance, the stage was set for a high-stakes encounter where every decision could prove decisive. Tactical Stalemate in the Opening Period On August 29, 2026 , the match began with Coventry looking to establish early dominance. Taiwo Awoniyi and Ephron Mason-Clark were active in the final third, though their efforts were frequently thwarted by the assistant referee’s flag. Hull City remained disciplined, though Lewie Coyle was forced into an early yellow card in the 10th minute to halt a dangerous counter-attack. As the first half progressed, both sides struggled to find their rhythm in front of goal. Defensive lapses from Matt Grimes and Loum Tchaouna briefly threatened to break the deadlock, but neither side could capitalize. Despite Coventry controlling much of the territory, the teams headed into the tunnel with the scoreline still level, setting the scene for a tense second half. Millar Breaks the Deadlock The second half saw a flurry of tactical adjustments and a rising count of cautions as Regan Slater and Elliot Stroud entered the book. Coventry continued to boss the possession, eventually reaching 69%, but they lacked the clinical edge required to beat Konstantinos Tzolakis . The game turned in the 82nd minute when substitute Liam Millar made his mark. Following an assist from Mohamed Belloumi , Liam Millar found space to strike with his right foot, sending the ball into the back of the net. It was a clinical finish that rewarded Hull City ’s patience and defensive resilience, leaving the home side shell-shocked after controlling so much of the play. Late Pressure and Hull’s Resilience In a frantic finish, Coventry City threw everything forward. During five minutes of added time, Jay Dasilva saw a goal-bound header brilliantly saved by Tzolakis , while Taiwo Awoniyi was again denied by an offside call. Despite the late aerial dominance of Aurele Amenda and Brandon Thomas-Asante , Hull City held firm to secure a narrow victory, snatching all three points in a display of gritty defensive organization."
